<title>BELGIUM: Fischler says EU wheat tax a &quot;precautionary&quot; move.</title>
<headline>Fischler says EU wheat tax a &quot;precautionary&quot; move.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union tax on the export of wheat grain, flour and semolina is a precautionary measure to avoid an overheating of the EU cereals market, Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The introduction of this tax is necessary to stabilise wheat prices,&quot; Fischler said in a statement after the EU's executive commission approved the tax.</p>
<p>In recent weeks, prices have been increasing due to a generally low level of world stocks and uncertainty about EU and world harvests caused by climatic factors, Fischler said.  </p>
<p>Fischler added that the European Commission was responsible for preventing prices rising too high as well as preventing them falling too low.</p>
<p>The Commission set the following export taxes, which may be adjusted in the light of market developments (Ecus/tonne):</p>
<p>    - durum wheat		 10.0</p>
<p>    - common wheat		15.0</p>
<p>    - durum wheat flour	 15.0</p>
<p>    - common wheat flour	20.0</p>
<p>    - durum wheat semolina    15.0</p>
<p>    - common wheat semolina   20.0</p>
<p>--Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
